      "role": "fe",
      "roleName": "Front-end",
      "years": 5.0,
      "text": "I would say all skills will still be very relevant. AI, as of today, is a fantastic accelerator to getting things done. - Yet, since it's nowhere near as reliable as one would hope, with no real sign of improving in that regard, I don't see it making any particular skill obsolete.\n\nThe primary issue with AI is the lack of self confidence assessment. An AI has thus far always interacted with developers with the sound of outmost confidence; leading to bad code and subpar quality of work. Humans must learn today to gauge an AI's answers instead of having the AI communicate that \"its unsure\" itself."
