      "cat": "fund",
      "role": "fs",
      "roleName": "Full-stack",
      "years": null,
      "text": "Security, best practices, embedded/low level programming and I still think most general programming skills will still be necessary. AI is trained on people's data. People make mistakes. I don't trust AI to generate better code unless people have already made it. I've caught AI failing to close files before, and I don't trust it to really get better. My understanding is that it isn't particularly good at low-level programming, and I suspect that any learning curve there will be slower than in other areas. However, I have limited experience as of yet, and haven't really tried using AI with HDLs, which I have done a little more of."
