      "roleName": "Full-stack",
      "years": 28.0,
      "text": "\"more capable\" than what? AI tools have a fundamental design flaw because they are all an attempt to pass the Turing Test. In other words: these tools are trained to fool humans into believing that they are human. They are not and never will be. They are like successful politicians: lying  convincingly to gain trust and we encourage them, either fascinated by the technology or looking for a way to transfer responsibility outside of ourselves. What we lose are our own unique skills, our ownership, our responsibilities, our courage, our expression. We slide voluntarily into our pods in the matrix, forgetting what we are here for. All our skills are and remain valuable. I do not have them to work, I have them to help me fulfil my goal in life."
