      "years": 27.0,
      "text": "A few years ago I heard the AI will be a big revolution in coding, but actually, even today, it is mainly a smarter autocomplete, google-search, or boiler-plate generator of a code that is easy to generate but hard to maintain in the long run. At least for my applications. And I don't see it is really becoming so much helpful as the hype around would suggest. So I am not sure if much changes in case of designing, understanding how the stuff works under the hood, diagnose/debug real complex issues, etc. My impression is that most optimistic visions are spread by sellers or influencers who don't use it on daily basis but only talk about coding. But let's what happens. If it really improves I should notice that quickly."
