      "sub": "adapt_learn",
      "cat": "adapt",
      "role": "fs",
      "roleName": "Full-stack",
      "years": 2.0,
      "text": "The ability to learn and understand how and why things work.  Whether AI-generated or not, there will always be a need to figure out how code works and have the sense of if something is wrong with it.  Also, that allows you to recognize when something is correct, but incomplete, which can be far more dangerous than it being wrong.\n\nThe ability to think about how the code will be used in ways that don't align with its intended design or original purpose is also something that is likely more predictable by humans than AI.  This can lead to problems if the codebase can't be adapted and it's forced into tasks that it's not capable of performing."
