      "text": "Knowing how to code is still important. You can give a man a fishing pole but if you don't teach him how to fish there's no point. AI is a generative tool that still has no idea what it's doing. It's driven on predictions and needs to be told exactly what to do to be used effectively. If you don't know exactly what to do, you're going to be writing poor unmaintainable code."
