      "text": "LLMs are only capable of generating what has already been created and they are never going to be 100% accurate. Developing new coding patterns or adopting new syntax will require humans to write the code. I also think in 3–5 years we are going to have many code bases that are a hot mess from folks trying to get LLMs to generate the code for them uncritically and we will need a lot of really smart people to clean it up."
