      "cat": "problem",
      "role": "be",
      "roleName": "Back-end",
      "years": 4.0,
      "text": "While I have a strict personal stance on not using AI, I do believe they're useful tools. I believe the role of average developers will likely shift most of the writing code they do to much more reading and verifying code and test cases. Code written by AI should be vetted just as much, if not more so, than code written by a person. It needs to be read by a human. So unless people are just committing whatever their AI throws at them thoughlessly, I think roles will switch to lots of reading code."
