      "text": "I don't know. I'm surrounded by brilliant people whose entire academic career is making AI better, so if they can make their creations output as creative and productive as they are, then AI could continue supplanting itself into everything. For developers specifically, in my experience, you can have much more depth in knowledge and vastly more contextual awareness than any AI I've used. I think you need to dig deeper when learning to write better code, because AI can produce the same stuff as someone who doesn't care."
