      "roleName": "Full-stack",
      "years": 6.0,
      "text": "Memorization of easily looked up algorithms, boilerplate, and so on will become an obsolete party-favor more so than a skill that can be used to get ahead professionally. Front end will be most impacted, back end still has a ways to go from what I've seen. Most front end devs will have to become full stack or risk absolute job insecurity"
