      "sub": "domain_product",
      "cat": "domain",
      "role": "be",
      "roleName": "Back-end",
      "years": 7.0,
      "text": "ability to see the whole picture of creating the app = architecture, performance, clean code, extensibility, test coverage. I think a person can make a decision about what technologies should be used for a given solution. Ability to create a complex system, which an application is. Ability to communicate with the customer and see potential problems. Ability to think about the business requirement and asking the customer to specify it better, knowing what is a complete or incomplete requirement. Ability to think in the style what should happen if there is invalid user input value, how should the code handle it? The developer tries to build a robust solution, so he knows he must validate the inputs, think about edge cases, he must write solid e2e tests to consider all scenarios etc. Developer knows what is important to handle and what is a detail which does not need much attention. Developer can explain what the application does."
