      "cat": "fund",
      "role": "be",
      "roleName": "Back-end",
      "years": 1.0,
      "text": "Fundamental ability to solve problems on your own. No matter how much data is piped into these LLMs they're still not going to understand nuanced problems. They don't reason, they pretend to reason by predicting text. They can be really useful for generating examples, automating repetitive boilerplate tasks, or understanding a codebase / documentation, but they will never replace developers themselves.\nThey support developers, not replace them."
