      "cat": "problem",
      "role": "fs",
      "roleName": "Full-stack",
      "years": 21.0,
      "text": "Debugging and creating elegant code. An example of elegant code is knowing when it's better to use a list comprehension vs. nested for-loops depending upon the use case. AI doesn't catch that type of nuance (yet ;-). On the other hand, hardware and language improvements are making that type of decision more and more obsolete."
