      "roleName": "Data/ML",
      "years": 3.0,
      "text": "'- Critical thinking.\n- Being able to solve very specific problems AND to search for information in parallel (models always fail when their train data is not up to date, and it seems that their \"search in the web\" function does not apply to most recent documentation online).\n- Debugging code. For some reason, AI tends to be stubborn on some topics (specially when its training data does not have most recent versions of APIs, etc) and indulgent on others (you can trick it very easily saying \"it doesn't work\" or \"you're wrong\")"
