      "text": "I believe exactly the same tools will remain valuable that are valuable today. In regards to software development, I believe the only persistent change that will be brought about by LLMs will be the devaluation of the knowledge bank that is the internet, and none the least fora like Stack Overflow, where I fear that LLM-generated crap will completely overflow all the contents that has been collected, sorted and pruned by the community over the past decades.\n\nI don't see any arguments why a machine that can predict the next written language token would be good for creating software. And so far, I haven't seen any examples to prove it - quite the contrary."
