      "text": "Understanding complex systems - code generators can handle bits and pieces, but can't be trusted to ask the right questions in order to satisfy a customer's request to \"modernize my existing application stack while resolving outstanding bugs.\"\n\nDebugging and bug hunting - already well documented.\n\nRequirements gathering - if a customer comes to me asking to \"build a web application to replace my existing desktop app,\" I rely on years of experience building and maintaining software systems in order to know which follow-up questions to ask, and when to push back on naive requests in order to guide the customer to a solution that actually meets their needs.  I have zero confidence that any LLM is going to match that skillset - ever."
