      "roleName": "Full-stack",
      "years": 25.0,
      "text": "The ability to analyse problems and make important engineering decisions, taking into account the context of the organization and the people that work there. \n\nOrganizations and customers are fundamentally still comprised of humans, and AI tools are incapable of understanding what really makes them tick.\n\nFundamental engineering knowledge - systems design, coding techniques and algorithms - will remain important. AI can regurgitate these, sure, but the skill isn't in parroting them, but rather in knowing how to make decisions about which to use."
