      "text": "I think you can use AI tools most effective if you are already an expert in the field, so that you have a good intuition whether an answer can be trusted or not. For instance, when AI codes there are often subtle bugs. If you know what to look out for they can often easily be fixed. But with no or little experience (junior devs) chances are that you just take the code as it seems to work, but will cause trouble later.\nAI also helps to ask for a quick overview of new technological areas, but I wouldn't trust it to be my sole source of information. Generally speaking, I think you have to already know stuff to use AI safely and efficiently."
